<Prose title="Shot and other screenshot apps" description="What Shot does and doesn't do, and when another Mac screenshot app is a better fit.">
  <h1>Shot and other screenshot apps</h1>
  <p>Your Mac already takes screenshots, and several apps do more. Shot is a menu bar app for taking a screenshot, marking it up and pasting it. This page says what that covers and what it doesn't, so you can tell whether Shot is the right one for you.</p>

  <h2>Pick Shot if you want</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The keys you already know.</strong> <kbd>⌘⇧4</kbd> takes a screenshot, with Tab to switch between an area, a window and the whole screen, and <kbd>⌘⇧5</kbd> records. The picture is copied and saved the moment you let go.</li>
    <li><strong>Marking up without leaving the corner card.</strong> After every capture a card appears in the corner. Add arrows, text, sticky notes, highlights, blur or pixelate, or drag the capture straight into another app.</li>
    <li><strong>Recordings and GIFs.</strong> Record an area, a window or a screen with your microphone, your Mac's sound and a camera bubble. Trim, cut and speed up the recording, then export an MP4 or a GIF.</li>
    <li><strong>Text from the screen.</strong> Drag out an area and Shot copies the words in it, read on your Mac.</li>
    <li><strong>Long pages in one screenshot.</strong> Drag out the part of the screen that scrolls and scroll it yourself. Shot stitches the frames as you go, in any direction, and keeps a sticky header or a pinned column once.</li>
    <li><strong>No account, no cloud, no analytics.</strong> Shot goes online only to check for updates, after it asks. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Free, open source software.</strong> The <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/shot">code is on GitHub</a> under the GPL-3.0 license, with no ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pick something else if you want</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Scrolling capture that scrolls for you.</strong> Shot builds the picture while you scroll, and never moves the page itself. <a href="https://cleanshot.com">CleanShot X</a> and <a href="https://shottr.cc">Shottr</a> can scroll some apps on their own, which needs the Accessibility permission.</li>
    <li><strong>Share links.</strong> Shot keeps your captures on your Mac and has no upload or link sharing. CleanShot X shares captures through its own cloud, and Shottr can upload to S3-compatible storage once you activate it.</li>
    <li><strong>Only what macOS already does.</strong> The built-in Screenshot tool (<kbd>⌘⇧5</kbd>) takes screenshots and recordings, has a timer, and lets you mark up or trim from its thumbnail. If that's enough, you don't need another app. It has no GIF export.</li>
    <li><strong>An older macOS.</strong> Shot needs macOS 15 or later, and it runs only on the Mac.</li>
    <li><strong>An app that's finished.</strong> Shot is in beta. It works, and it's still being built.</li>
    <li><strong>An app Apple has notarized.</strong> Shot isn't notarized yet, so macOS blocks it the first time you open it, and the <a href="/#install">install steps</a> show how to open it anyway.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These other apps change their features and prices, so check each one's own site before you decide.</p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>Shot needs macOS 15 or later, on Apple Silicon or Intel. Install it with <code>brew install lorcanchinnock/tap/shot</code>, or <a href="/download">download the zip</a>. <a href="/docs/get-started/">Get started</a> covers the first launch.</p>
</Prose>
